ion\",\n      \"description\": \"Mainstream expert opinions are the generally accepted views of professionals and experts in various fields.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Popular Culture\",\n      \"type\": \"Culture\",\n      \"description\": \"Popular culture encompasses the cultural elements that are prevalent or dominant in a society, including media, entertainment, and public discourse.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Assassination of President John F. Kennedy\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Event\",\n      \"description\": \"The assassination of President John F. Kennedy occurred on November 22, 1963, in Dallas, Texas. Kennedy was fatally shot while traveling through the city in a presidential motorcade.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Public Discourse\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"Public discourse refers to the collective conversation and exchange of ideas within a community or society, often influencing public opinion and policy.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Official Explanations\",\n      \"type\": \"Narrative\",\n      \"description\": \"Official explanations are the accounts or narratives provided by recognized authorities or institutions regarding events or phenomena.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Sense of Empowerment\",\n      \"type\": \"Emotional State\",\n      \"description\": \"A sense of empowerment is a feeling of having control or influence over one\\\"s environment or circumstances.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Community\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Group\",\n      \"description\": \"A community is a group of people with a common interest or characteristic, often interacting and supporting each other.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"conspiracy theories\",\n      \"type\": \"Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"Conspiracy theories are speculative explanations for events that are believed to be planned and executed in secret by powerful groups or individuals.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"official narratives\",\n      \"type\": \"Information\",\n      \"description\": \"Official narratives are the accepted or mainstream explanations of events, often provided by governments or authoritative institutions.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"societal anxieties\",\n      \"type\": \"Emotion\",\n      \"description\": \"Societal anxieties are widespread feelings of unease or worry within a community or society, often related to economic, political, or social issues.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"distrust of authority\",\n      \"type\": \"Emotion\",\n      \"description\": \"Distrust of authority is a lack of confidence in the integrity and intentions of those in positions of power, such as government officials or corporate leaders.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sense of empowerment\",\n      \"type\": \"Emotion\",\n      \"description\": \"A sense of empowerment is the feeling of having the ability to influence or control one\\\"s environment or circumstances.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"human desire for alternative explanations\",\n      \"type\": \"Psychological Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"The human desire for alternative explanations is a cognitive tendency to seek out and believe in explanations that differ from the official or mainstream accounts.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"public discourse\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"Public discourse refers to the collective discussions and debates that occur within a society, often shaping public opinion and policy.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"investigations\",\n      \"type\": \"Process\",\n      \"description\": \"Investigations are systematic inquiries or examinations aimed at uncovering facts or solving problems.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"documentaries\",\n      \"type\": \"Media\",\n      \"description\": \"Documentaries are non-fiction films or television programs that aim to document reality, often for the purposes of instruction, education, or maintaining a historical record.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"space race\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Event\",\n      \"description\": \"The space race was a 20th-century competition between the United States and the Soviet Union to achieve superior spaceflight capability.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"mystery and intrigue\",\n      \"type\": \"Emotional State\",\n      \"description\": \"Mystery and intrigue are emotional states that arise from the unknown and the unexplained, often attracting people to explore deeper.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"relations\": [\n    [\n      \"Conspiracy Theories\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"Moon Landing Hoax Theory\",\n      \"The moon landing hoax theory is one of the most famous conspiracy theories, often discussed and debated despite overwhelming scientific evidence to the contrary.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Conspiracy Theories\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"JFK Assassination Theory\",\n      \"The JFK assassination theory is a well-known conspiracy theory that has led to numerous investigations, documentaries, and speculations, keeping the theory alive to this day.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Conspiracy Theories\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"9/11 Conspiracy Theory\",\n      \"The 9/11 conspiracy theory is another famous theory that has gained widespread attention and followers, often pointing to alleged inconsistencies in the official accounts of th